  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, the controls to set the profile visibility of a group that you're in, only appear AFTER you join the group.  For a group with open membership, that isn't too bad, because it'd be a matter of seconds between joining and tweaking the visibility to your liking; but for a group where your membership has to be APPROVED, they might approve you in the middle of (your) night, and you won't have a chance to find out and change the visibility settings until morning (meaning, the group will be visible on your profile for hours, in the meantime.)\n\nThe simplest way to address this would be to have all group memberships default to hidden until specified otherwise, but I could understand if you were worried that that would interfere with groups' ability to spread or whatever.\n\nSo if not that, the simplest solution would probably be to just make the visibility setting accessible even if you *aren't* in a group yet, with the chosen value being applied automatically once you are?   (Or, maybe the visibility choice comes up as part of the join request UI?)",
